spruce has no real 'null' operator: any unknown operator name falls back to NullOperator{Missing: name}, which for a zero-arg call is special-cased at operator.go:626 to leave the marker text unresolved (literal (( null )) survives in output) rather than erroring. graft registers 'null' as a real operator that evaluates to the YAML null value. This is a graft-only extension beyond spruce's operator set, confirmed against spruce source (no op_null-equivalent registration exists), not a parity bug.
